Merger Agreement Excerpt: “Material Impediment” means any event, circumstance, or effect that singularly or in combination would materially impair the operational capability of the Company, including its ability to consummate the Transaction contemplated hereby. Notwithstanding the broad scope of this definition, for determining a Material Impediment, the following exceptions shall not be taken into account: (i) general shifts in market sentiment or pervasive economic downturns, (ii) routine modifications in regulatory or tax regimes that do not uniquely affect the Company’s principal operational assets, (iii) isolated or mutually agreed upon administrative or communication delays, and (iv) adjustments in internal accounting policies unless such adjustments result in a disproportionately adverse effect compared with industry norms. Importantly, any adverse effect that specifically hinders the Company’s ability to consummate the Transaction shall not fall within these exceptions.
